cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this repository helps you, you may cite it as below. It is an informal,
  work-in-progress synthesis of published research, written with Claude, an AI
  assistant by Anthropic. It is not an official standard, not peer-reviewed,
  and not a new result.
title: "ai-augmented-foundations (work in progress)"
abstract: >-
  Whether the family's setup is complete and whether it converges: can a tree or graph of topics encode every problem at a cognitive cost a person bears; how fast a project reaches a result, acceptable or optimal, and what an optimum is. A first review pass in two topics and a candidate cost of a tree of topics are written.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tewf"
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-11-04
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tewf/ai-augmented-foundations"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - expressiveness
  - cognitive load
  - satisficing
  - optimal stopping
  - multi-objective optimisation
  - literature review
